Writer: the first layout of a long document is no longer quadratic in its number of paragraphs.

SwTextFrame::Format() collected every following frame of the next-chain into a vector before each
FormatImpl() call, to order the anchors of objects that FormatImpl() reports as intersecting the
paragraph. Until the layout has moved them to their pages, all remaining paragraphs of a newly loaded
document are in that chain, so the first layout was O(paragraphs^2): a 50 MB plain text file of short
Vietnamese lines (about 550 000 paragraphs) loaded in about 20 s and then kept the office at 100 % CPU
in idle layout for more than 15 minutes (the "never finishes opening" report), every stack sample in
that loop. A 10 MB file still settled in 8 s, which is why smaller files looked fine.

FormatImpl() can report intersecting objects only when SwTextFly is on, which needs anchored objects
on the paragraph's page (SwTextFly::CtorInitTextFly: m_bOn = page->GetSortedObjs() != nullptr). The
next-chain is now collected only in that case, so pages with pictures, frames or shapes behave as
before and plain text no longer pays for it.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_large_file_open_patches.py; runtime: scripts/perf/large-file-open-local.sh with
the text-*-50mb.txt fixtures (docs/PERFORMANCE_LARGE_FILES.md); sw layout CppunitTests.

